{"author":{"id":"60e8a4f6c4ac173f9427846756ea0ba4ba542d61e99b8bc2fc9c99440a92cf8c"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795252398,"nonce":"cURPpuDfYmpuNGDpg/1BdVB6c9c=","title":"Check on a run that the cadence estimate and stride length look right","message":"The first test run (2026-11-18) showed that a Garmin records the footpod's cadence of 0 as 0 spm\ninstead of falling back to wrist cadence, which also zeroes running power and running dynamics.\nCadence is a mandatory RSC field, so it cannot be left out.\n\nThe engine now estimates cadence from speed with one fixed curve (with a separate walking range below\nabout 6–7 km/h), and sends it as strides per minute, since Garmin reads RSC cadence that way, with\nstride length as a full two-step stride.\n\nCheck on a run: cadence matches the curve, stride length looks like a step, and walking breaks count\nas walking again.","files":null}]}